<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The Hemophage's helmet, on VFEP's helmet base (VFEP v4.03,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Headgear.xml). The research gate, the absent
    apparel tags, the text's shape and the masked tint follow the armor's header
    (Warcasket_Hemophage.xml).

    Tuning: the set's heaviest plating, on the tier's baseline. Sharp 2 is the tier's and
    the stat's maximum. Blunt 1.5 is the Guardian's and the Brute's specialty, the most any
    VFEP piece carries, and Combat Extended has a row for it. Heat 2 is the stat's maximum and
    the Hazard's on every piece: flame damage arrives without armor penetration, so none of
    it gets through to the head. Mass 8, PsychicSensitivity -0.5, ToxicResistance 0.5,
    SlaveSuppressionOffset 0.1, VacuumResistance 0.7 and uiIconScale 1.25 are the same on
    all five of VFEP's spacer helmets. Insulation 10 / 10 is three of the five's (Controller,
    Sarcophagus, Brute; the Siegebreaker's and the Guardian's are 5 / 2).

    Cost: ComponentSpacer 4 is the tier's price for a helmet with a function of its own (the
    Controller's and the Brute's, where the other three take 2), here the visor's two.
    Plasteel 70 is the Guardian helmet's, what VFEP charges for Blunt 1.5. DevilstrandCloth
    30 pays for the heat plating in the Hazard's currency: its armor takes 100 and its shoulders 50 for the same Heat 2. The
    Hazard's own helmet takes none, so the 30 is this set's price, a helmet's share at that
    rate.

    Sunlight: the SunlightShieldExtension keeps a sunlight sensitivity gene's effects off the
    pilot (Source/1.6/Sunlight/SunlightShield.cs has which, and the patches that do it). It
    is all or nothing because the genes' effects are: a factor and a thought that are either
    on or off. blocksSunlight is the settings' switch.

    Pyrophobia: the PyrophobiaReliefExtension lets half of the fire terror breaks of
    Biotech's FireTerror gene through (Source/1.6/Fire/PyrophobiaRelief.cs has the
    mechanic), which doubles the gene's mean time near a fire from 0.1 days to 0.2, about
    100 seconds at normal speed to about 200. The pilot is as afraid as ever and slower to
    bolt, for being harder to burn. It sits on the helmet as the set's most fireproof piece
    and beside the visor's other protection. breakChanceFactor is the settings' slider, down
    to 0 for a pilot who never bolts.

    Art: the back of the helmet has no black-masked part, so its glow sprite for the _north
    facing is an empty image. Graphic_Multi fills a missing north facing from the south one,
    which would light the eyes on the back of the head. The glow node follows the armor's
    header.

    ApparelExtension priority 1, for the reason in the armor's header; Merge still ORs the
    base's isUnifiedApparel and hideHead in. Any new ApparelExtension field for the helmet
    goes on this entry.

    Patched by 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml (EVA tag, Insulation_Cold 100), the VGE vacuum patch
    (VGE1's warcasket-helmet VacuumResistance) and the 1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root
    (plating on CE's scale, bulk, smoke sealing, costs); see their headers.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase">
    <defName>HPWC_WarcasketHelmet_Hemophage</defName>
    <label>hemophage warcasket helmet</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with improved impact dispersion and heat protection, equipped with a visor that shields the pilot from sunlight and makes them less likely to flee from fire.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with improved impact dispersion and heat protection, equipped with a visor that shields the pilot from sunlight and makes them less likely to flee from fire.\n\nThe 10th generation came out of a government program that rebuilt captured pirate rigs around its own power armor and gave them to veterans who could no longer serve any other way. The program has no record of a Hemophage series. Some think the designs were stolen and refitted for sanguophages. Some believe the series was sanctioned in secret from the top of the program, which sanguophages had directed all along.\n\nThe Hemophage series runs on its pilot's hemogen. Injectors in the shell keep the pilot's blood pumping even without a heart, and can spend their hemogen quickly to make them much faster and stronger. Servos in the pauldrons can tear a limb off an enemy and leave a wound the pilot can feed from, and the helmet keeps out sunlight and helps the pilot hold their nerve near fire. For a non-hemogenic pilot this series is somewhat lackluster, but it suits a sanguophage who prefers to fight up close.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketHemophage/WarcasketHemophageHelmet</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <uiIconScale>1.25</uiIconScale>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>8</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1.5</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>2</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>10</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>10</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.1</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.7</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>4</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>70</Plasteel>
      <DevilstrandCloth>30</DevilstrandCloth>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>FullHead</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketHemophage/WarcasketHemophageHelmet</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <renderNodeProperties>
        <li>
          <debugLabel>HPWC_HemogenGlow</debugLabel>
          <nodeClass>HemophageWarcasket.PawnRenderNode_HemogenGlow</nodeClass>
          <workerClass>HemophageWarcasket.PawnRenderNodeWorker_HemogenGlow</workerClass>
          <parentTagDef>ApparelHead</parentTagDef>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketHemophage/WarcasketHemophageHelmetGlow</texPath>
          <shaderTypeDef>TransparentPostLight</shaderTypeDef>
          <color>(1, 0.2, 0.15)</color>
        </li>
      </renderNodeProperties>
      <layers>
        <li>Overhead</li>
      </layers>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
      </li>
      <li Class="HemophageWarcasket.SunlightShieldExtension">
        <blocksSunlight>true</blocksSunlight>
      </li>
      <li Class="HemophageWarcasket.PyrophobiaReliefExtension">
        <breakChanceFactor>0.5</breakChanceFactor>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
